\n\nVectors BD = (1 - a, -b), BE = (2 - a, -b)\n\nDot product BD \u22c5 BE = (1 - a)(2 - a) + (-b)(-b) = (2 - a - 2a + a\u00b2) + b\u00b2 = (2 - 3a + a\u00b2) + b\u00b2\n\n|BD| = sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)\n\n|BE| = sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)\n\nThus,\n\ncos(angle DBE) = (2 - 3a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) / [sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)]\n\nAngle EBC between BE and BC.\n\nVectors BE = (2 - a, -b), BC = (3 - a, -b)\n\nDot product BE \u22c5 BC = (2 - a)(3 - a) + (-b)(-b) = (6 - 2a - 3a + a\u00b2) + b\u00b2 = (6 - 5a + a\u00b2) + b\u00b2\n\n|BE| = sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)\n\n|BC| = sqrt((3 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)\n\nSo,\n\ncos(angle EBC) = (6 - 5a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) / [sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((3 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)]\n\nWe need all three cosines to be equal. That is:\n\n[ (-a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ] = [ (2 - 3a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ] = [ (6 - 5a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((3 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ]\n\nThis seems quite complex. Maybe we can set up equations by equating the first two expressions and then the second and third.\n\nLet me denote:\n\nC1 = [ (-a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ]\n\nC2 = [ (2 - 3a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ]\n\nC3 = [ (6 - 5a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((3 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ]\n\nWe need C1 = C2 and C2 = C3.\n\nLet me first set C1 = C2:\n\n[ (-a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ] = [ (2 - 3a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) ] / [ sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) ]\n\nWe can cancel sqrt((1 - a)^2 + b\u00b2) from both sides:\n\n(-a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) / sqrt(a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) = (2 - 3a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) / sqrt((2 - a)^2 + b\u00b2)\n\nCross-multiplying:\n\n(-a + a\u00b2 + b\u00b2) * sqrt((2 - a