al (perpendicular to x-axis), passing through (d, 0). Points B and C are (d, t) and (d, -t), since A\u2081 is the midpoint.\n\nThe circle centered at O with radius R has equation x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 = R\u00b2. Since B and C are on this circle:\n\nd\u00b2 + t\u00b2 = R\u00b2 \u21d2 t = \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2)\n\nTherefore, points B = (d, \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2)), C = (d, -\u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2)).\n\nNow, we need to find point A = (x, y) on the circle x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 = R\u00b2 such that:\n\n1. The midpoint of AB lies on l\u2082, and l\u2082 is perpendicular to AB.\n\n2. The midpoint of AC lies on l\u2083, and l\u2083 is perpendicular to AC.\n\nLet\u2019s first handle condition 1.\n\nMidpoint of AB: M = ((x + d)/2, (y + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/2)\n\nThis midpoint must lie on l\u2082. Let\u2019s assume l\u2082 has equation y = m\u2082 x (passing through O).\n\nTherefore, substituting into l\u2082:\n\n(y + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/2 = m\u2082 (x + d)/2\n\nMultiply both sides by 2:\n\ny + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = m\u2082 (x + d)\n\nAlso, l\u2082 is perpendicular to AB. The slope of AB is (y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(x - d). Therefore, the slope of l\u2082 (m\u2082) must be the negative reciprocal:\n\nm\u2082 = - (x - d)/(y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))\n\nSimilarly, for condition 2:\n\nMidpoint of AC: N = ((x + d)/2, (y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/2)\n\nThis must lie on l\u2083: y = m\u2083 x\n\nTherefore:\n\n(y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/2 = m\u2083 (x + d)/2\n\nMultiply by 2:\n\ny - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = m\u2083 (x + d)\n\nAnd the slope of AC is (y + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(x - d), so the slope of l\u2083 (m\u2083) is the negative reciprocal:\n\nm\u2083 = - (x - d)/(y + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))\n\nNow, we have four equations:\n\n1. x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 = R\u00b2\n\n2. y + \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = m\u2082 (x + d)\n\n3. m\u2082 = - (x - d)/(y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2))\n\n4. y - \u221a(R\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = m\u2083 (x + d)\n\n5. m\u2083 =